egas Sands Corp., together with its subsidiaries, owns, develops, and operates integrated resorts in Macao and Singapore. It owns and operates The Venetian Macao Resort Hotel, The Londoner Macao, The Parisian Macao, The Plaza Macao and Four Seasons Hotel Macao, and The Sands Macao in Macao, the People's Republic of China; and Marina Bay Sands in Singapore. The company's integrated resorts feature accommodations, gaming, entertainment and retail malls, convention and exhibition facilities, celebrity chef restaurants, and other amenities. The company was founded in 1988 and is based in Las Vegas, Nevada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Patrick  Dumont | Chairman, CEO, President & Treasurer | Age 50 | Compensation: $13.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 41K people. Revenue per employee of $317K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $45K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 43\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Las Vegas Sands Corp. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $25.3B market cap on $13.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +47% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 7% cost of capital, a 9-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $1.9B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.86\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.8\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 12.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 64% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (18.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.9M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3910659.75},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 13% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 14% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 27% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 21% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Las Vegas Sands (LVS) A Bargain After Its New Shelf Registration?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-services/nyse-lvs/las-vegas-sands/news/is-las-vegas-sands-lvs-a-bargain-after-its-new-shelf-registr","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794468421.178,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.872,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Trading the Move, Not the Narrative: (LVS) Edition","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/52/Trading_the_Move,_Not_the_Narrative:_LVS_Edition_110826065202_1794181922.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794181922.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"38,740 Las Vegas Sands Corp. $LVS Shares Sold by Sumitomo Mitsui Trust Group Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/38740-las-vegas-sands-corp-lvs-shares-sold-by-sumitomo-mitsui-trust-group-inc.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793959671.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.964,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Las Vegas Sands (NYSE:LVS) Stock Price Breaks Above 50 Day Moving Average After Analyst Downgrade","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/las-vegas-sands-nyselvs-stock-price-breaks-above-50-day-moving-average-after-analyst-downgrade.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793888127.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":